course: dictionary
lesson: 1402
title: Carbonates
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A carbonate is a chemical compound that contains carbon and oxygen, joined with another element such as calcium. «Eggshell and chalk are calcium carbonate.» So calcium carbonate is one kind of carbonate, found in chalk, limestone and eggshell.
explain: Carbonates react with acids. «Eggshell is calcium carbonate; in vinegar it fizzes away over days.» When an acid like vinegar touches a carbonate, it fizzes and gives off carbon dioxide gas. That fizzing is a clue that a rock or shell may be a carbonate.
explain: Carbonate can also be a verb. To carbonate a drink means to add carbon dioxide gas to it so that it fizzes. That is why fizzy drinks are called carbonated drinks.
fact: A carbonate contains carbon and oxygen.
fact: Chalk and limestone are both calcium carbonate.
fact: Carbonates fizz when an acid such as vinegar is added, giving off carbon dioxide gas.
fact: «Chalk cliffs are made from the shells of countless tiny sea creatures.»
fact: Limescale, the white crust left by hard water when it is heated, is mostly calcium carbonate.
exercise: Which substance, found in chalk and limestone, is a carbonate? | Tap water | *Calcium carbonate | Carbon dioxide gas on its own | Vinegar
exercise: «Eggshell is calcium carbonate; in vinegar it fizzes away over days.» What makes the eggshell fizz? | Sunlight shining on the shell | The shell being cracked | *Vinegar, an acid, reacting with the carbonate | Water, because eggshell always fizzes in water
exercise: To carbonate a drink means what? | To cool it in a freezer | To pour it into a clean glass | *To add carbon dioxide gas so that it fizzes | To add sugar to make it sweet
test: Geologists test a rock with a drop of acid. If the rock fizzes, what does that suggest it may contain? | *Carbonate, such as calcium carbonate | Sand only | Oxygen only | Ice
test: Why does limescale fizz when vinegar is added? | *Limescale is mostly calcium carbonate, like chalk | Limescale is made of sugar | Limescale is wood | Limescale is hot water
exam: Which statement about carbonates is correct? | Carbonates never react with acids | *Calcium carbonate in chalk fizzes when acid such as vinegar is added | A carbonate is a gas that makes rocks hard | Carbonates are only found in fizzy drinks
